# =============================================================================
#  ARP.orch - Audio Recording Preservation (CAE-USC V2.5)
#  Workflow Description Language v0.3, AIF V3.0
#
#  One Controller, one Module, which executes continuously: the audio analysis and the video
#  analysis exchange the irregularities they find until they agree, so the Module is not run an
#  exchange at a time. The User Agent binds a device to every Port of the Module's boundary,
#  each to one Port, by Data Type and Port Number:
#
#    what the person gives the Module -
#      TapeIn        the digitised audio of the tape, as it was digitised (the Preservation Audio File)
#      FilmIn        the film of the playback head, with its audio (the Preservation Audio-Visual File)
#
#    what the Module gives -
#      AccessCopyOut      the Access Copy: the recording, restored where it needed it
#      MasterOut          the Preservation Master: the recording as it is, with the irregularities
#                         found, their images, the Editing List and a manifest
# =============================================================================

workflow ARP over 1CAE-ARP-V2.5-I01

on Start:

    ask Controller to start

    stream  TapeIn         (OSD-BAO-V1.5)   from device "TapeIn"
    stream  FilmIn         (OSD-BMO-V1.5)   from device "FilmIn"

    deliver AccessCopyOut  (OSD-BAO-V1.5:1) to device "AccessCopyOut"
    deliver MasterOut      (OSD-BAO-V1.5:2) to device "MasterOut"

    loop until Stop:
        wait 1s

on Stop:
    ask Controller to stop